-- title:
--   Volume of a closed cube of side $h$
-- statement:
--   For a real number $h$ and a point $u \in \mathbb{R}^d$, let $A_h(u) := \texttt{closedCube } h\ u$
--   denote the closed axis-parallel cube of side $h$ attached to $u$. Let $h \ge 0$. Then its Lebesgue
--   measure is
--
--   $$\lambda_d\big(A_h(u)\big) \;=\; h^{d},$$
--
--   as an element of $[0,\infty]$ (the right-hand side being `ENNReal.ofReal (h ^ d)`).
--
--   This is the normalising constant of the whole discretisation: the step approximation of a function
--   is $f_h(x) = h^{-d}\!\int_{A_h(x)} f$, and every conversion between a sum over lattice points and an
--   integral over $\mathbb{R}^d$ carries a factor $h^{d}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The hypothesis is only $h \ge 0$, so the degenerate case $h = 0$ is
--   included: the closed cube is then a single point, of measure $0 = 0^d$ when $d > 0$, and the whole
--   of the one-point space $\mathbb{R}^0$, of measure $1 = 0^0$, when $d = 0$. Both sides are elements
--   of `ℝ≥0∞`.
